# pnpm writes and deletes `_tmp_<pid>_<hex>` probe files in the directory it runs in. Nx's package-json
# plugin runs `pnpm --version` in every freshly spawned plugin worker (it only reads the top-level
# `packageManager` field, not `devEngines.packageManager`), so each graph recompute makes a probe
# whose deletion schedules the next recompute. The daemon never settles, `nx` commands hang, and
# daemon.log grows quadratically (21 GB in six hours here).
_tmp_*
